Good afternoon,

We are instructed to notify windstorm damage to the works at Cypress Landing Data Hall B. Our reference is SRR/BR/2025/1147.

Broker reference: SRR/BR/2025/1147
Project name: Cypress Landing Data Hall B
Contract number: CONSENSUSDOCS-410-2025-CLB
Insured name: Meridian Grid Holdings, LLC
Contractor: Ironbark Constructors, Inc.
Date of loss: 7 July 2026
Loss location: 14900 South Cypress Landing Way, Mesa, AZ 85212
Estimated loss: USD 5,900,000

A haboob and then a wet microburst crossed the site on Tuesday evening. The site
anemometer logged 78 mph. Two bays of steel racked, 4,400 sq ft of wall panel came
off and 9,200 sq ft of roof membrane lifted.

The serious element is that with the envelope open, two medium-voltage switchgear
line-ups sitting on their pads took blowing dust and then driving rain for about
ninety minutes. One is probably recoverable in the field; the other was struck by
a flying panel and looks like a factory re-manufacture with a 34 to 40 week lead.

Neither has been energised, opened or moved. Site evacuated at 18:26 and nobody
was hurt - 47 people were on site. This programme has no delay in start-up cover,
so any schedule consequence is a contractual matter between our client and the
contractor and is not tendered.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * electrical equipment assessment
  * storm damage schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and appoint an equipment expert quickly - the
switchgear is the whole exposure and it is sitting under a temporary cover.

Kind regards,

